    "body": "> Okay, so you want to distinguish between the service worker handing you a faulty response and the server handing you a faulty response, but no changes to respondWith() itself are planned? I guess that would help debugging, though architecturally it doesn't seem great to expose the existence of service workers.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I understand the comment. This happens when service worker has COEP: none and the page has COEP: require-corp, and it is tested in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/none-sw-from-require-corp.https.html.\r\n\r\n",
